{"title":"2021 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 16","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Vieta&#39;s_bash)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Vieta's bash)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Fakesolve)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Fakesolve)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(Good_at_Guessing)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (Good at Guessing)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(🚀Under_2_min_🚀)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (🚀Under 2 min 🚀)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Punxsutawney_Phil\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Punxsutawney Phil</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn_(Vieta&#39;s_Formula)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn (Vieta's Formula)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Hawk_Math\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Hawk Math</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">13</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/9/659a6a2610357101d77dbae8eb9bf0b3100c08fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" /> be a polynomial with leading coefficient <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/f/5bf27edd6ee0c25241392922eca9b9c9144f4d73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"17\" /> whose three roots are the reciprocals of the three roots of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/e/6beef82525b6dd8691405a91a4bfc718e35778b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)=x^3+ax^2+bx+c,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"202\" height=\"19\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/6/0b6c5cb84308f91ce1b52f96581c651d080f893f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1&lt;a&lt;b&lt;c.$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"110\" height=\"13\" /> What is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/e/cdedb884f0f68e277e3dd54525ecc72d6dfb09d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> in terms of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/b/f3b28547efd22be1c4a05fa193cd7038fc65d71b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"29\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/1/d21c935a6f845a1028685bffe28cc59f0a74c07e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c?$\" width=\"16\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/a/38aee3771db94c48fe7016cd5e359132ffb6ec18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }\\frac{1+a+b+c}c \\qquad \\textbf{(B) }1+a+b+c \\qquad \\textbf{(C) }\\frac{1+a+b+c}{c^2}\\qquad \\textbf{(D) }\\frac{a+b+c}{c^2} \\qquad \\textbf{(E) }\\frac{1+a+b+c}{a+b+c}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"796\" height=\"39\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/8/b8862155681335acbb528813a1563cbdcabd6bfe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(1/x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"52\" height=\"18\" /> has the same roots as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/9/659a6a2610357101d77dbae8eb9bf0b3100c08fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" />, if it is multiplied by some monomial so that the leading term is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/5/48524d3889ec8433cb03669176e738011df245b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^3$\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> they will be equal. We have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/4/d445d497c73df12477b4f7a987c8c3d844dd9e27.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(1/x) = \\frac{1}{x^3} + \\frac{a}{x^2}+\\frac{b}{x} + c\\]\" width=\"210\" height=\"37\" />\nso we can see that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/f/70f8e3089ec7eba045d932a0dff5250f7cc3a43c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[g(x) = \\frac{x^3}{c}f(1/x)\\]\" width=\"132\" height=\"39\" />\nTherefore\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/9/79989395b4413f6f007ecf21bbe70e43f9bf5984.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[g(1) = \\frac{1}{c}f(1) = \\boxed{\\textbf{(A) }\\frac{1+a+b+c}c}\\]\" width=\"280\" height=\"49\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Vieta.27s_bash.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Vieta's_bash)\">Solution 2 (Vieta's bash)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Vieta&#39;s bash)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the three roots of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/a/a3a59bb1293ee3f6dec19de4019a7178874219ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$e$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" />. (Here e does NOT mean 2.7182818...)\nWe know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/f/74fa167a7700b903832307c1e0ef5407659083c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=-(d+e+f)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"134\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/c/dcc01a85bfbfc8743fc0b564fc6a5b9a850e5722.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=de+ef+df$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"130\" height=\"16\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/4/0b49d1d61131dde0e6461289d375d836b76fd5d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c=-def$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"74\" height=\"16\" />, and that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/c/60ce6e9f6fa91128d94f82b178b7325f77b59eb3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(1)=1-\\frac{1}{d}-\\frac{1}{e}-\\frac{1}{f}+\\frac{1}{de}+\\frac{1}{ef}+\\frac{1}{df}-\\frac{1}{def}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"360\" height=\"40\" /> (Vieta's). This is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/b/82b381a27b9d5bf02ecf7d3267d3cd91bcee3ac4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{def-de-df-ef+d+e+f-1}{def}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"279\" height=\"41\" />, which equals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb25425a5e538dd0a1aa58b6e7eb3573b9e64d31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{(\\textbf{A}) \\frac{1+a+b+c}{c}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"145\" height=\"49\" />. -dstanz5\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Fakesolve.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Fakesolve)\">Solution 3 (Fakesolve)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Fakesolve)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Because the problem doesn't specify what the coefficients of the polynomial actually are, we can just plug in any arbitrary polynomial that satisfies the constraints. Let's take <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/c/dbccf8d10cd2c17789b38388a4c6fe546a0a8739.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) = (x+5)^3 = x^3+15x^2+75x+125$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"325\" height=\"21\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> has a triple root of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/f/6ef1c4328c03cd2021b41b653218a5778379397b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = -5$\" width=\"57\" height=\"12\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/9/659a6a2610357101d77dbae8eb9bf0b3100c08fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" /> has a triple root of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/1/e81dbf5b8287bd7bdc9c6f6d85dfbb47c9192d67.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-\\frac{1}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"25\" height=\"37\" />, and it's monic, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/e/dde31aada7c8addea539ba2b53dc25312333cf2f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(x) = \\left(x+\\frac{1}{5}\\right)^3 = \\frac{125x^3+75x^2+15x+1}{125}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"349\" height=\"46\" />. We can see that this is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/b/9fbca6ae1d36835ddfed5ded8e25eb457d4a2060.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1+a+b+c}{c}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"103\" height=\"37\" />, which is answer choice <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/4/70432e471002b1c1f363f2d085b0f3dff8d930a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{(A)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"39\" height=\"29\" />.\n</p><p>-Darren Yao\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If we let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/c/0ec2b6f850a38c18bff9b2d860b248982102966e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p, q,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"31\" height=\"11\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> be the roots of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/e/40ef06e3dedeab46a8b0fbd59d10710e424a9101.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) = (x-p)(x-q)(x-r)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"225\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/a/19a54fab8f05a70e2b19cb1703401b4b6d01877d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(x) = \\left(x-\\frac{1}{p}\\right)\\left(x-\\frac{1}{q}\\right)\\left(x-\\frac{1}{r}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"282\" height=\"45\" />. The requested value, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/e/cdedb884f0f68e277e3dd54525ecc72d6dfb09d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" />, is then\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/1/4c102fe238bb58dc9ecd1aa2b36940ffe969b73c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left(1-\\frac{1}{p}\\right)\\left(1-\\frac{1}{q}\\right)\\left(1-\\frac{1}{r}\\right) = \\frac{(p-1)(q-1)(r-1)}{pqr}\\]\" width=\"403\" height=\"43\" />\nThe numerator is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/0/1a055494e8d613f3da496e593649a6ca470e3df2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-f(1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"46\" height=\"18\" /> (using the product form of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> ) and the denominator is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/0/97038e79ad1870e413be597981d950ff4655bf2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-c$\" width=\"22\" height=\"8\" />, so the answer is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/3/91397baa415366721b5e0358b13495ef3eda03b3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{f(1)}{c} = \\boxed{(\\textbf{A}) \\frac{1+a+b+c}{c}}\\]\" width=\"205\" height=\"49\" />\n</p><p>- gting\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_5_.28Good_at_Guessing.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(Good_at_Guessing)\">Solution 5 (Good at Guessing)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (Good at Guessing)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The function <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/c/18c4b6ee5b1d40d40203d0d58d2a6b5297ac7c57.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(1) = \\text{sum of coefficients}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"191\" height=\"20\" />. If it's <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/4/dd4b208371da8ad3ffe81bc04f978c6da9067c62.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x-r)(x-s)(x-t)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"166\" height=\"20\" />, then it becomes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/1/341e018ab5696c1c8a68d9bb371e18e6e4dcffa5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x-\\dfrac{1}{r})(x-\\dfrac{1}{s})(x-\\dfrac{1}{t}).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"186\" height=\"38\" />\nSo, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/8/7287d9b8ec3ea2dd94dc2cab730e16c84989e45b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-rst$\" width=\"37\" height=\"11\" /> becomes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6eec00b1e0a65b839669684b818b74de5d75a018.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-\\dfrac{1}{rst}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"44\" height=\"38\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> becomes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/0/60078e731e22d107c1f396f073a9cd8f4b26a5f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{1}{c}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" />. Also, there is a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/5/48524d3889ec8433cb03669176e738011df245b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^3$\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> so the answer must include <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. The only answer having both of these is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>~smellyman\n</p><p>-Extremelysupercooldude (Minor Latex Edits and Grammar)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6\">Solution 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>It is well known that reversing the order of the coefficients of a polynomial turns each root into its corresponding reciprocal. Thus, a polynomial with the desired roots may be written as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/8/2486eb07bddb23004a465116d7833e0d12679f1a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$cx^3+bx^2+a+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"139\" height=\"18\" />. As the problem statement asks for a monic polynomial, our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/6/c3675274907c7c790d1e2fb5a8ba11308c5043d2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\boxed{(\\textbf{A}) \\frac{1+a+b+c}{c}}\\]\" width=\"145\" height=\"49\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28.F0.9F.9A.80Under_2_min_.F0.9F.9A.80.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(🚀Under_2_min_🚀)\">Video Solution (🚀Under 2 min 🚀)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (🚀Under 2 min 🚀)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/vPw6VxuZvQU\">https://youtu.be/vPw6VxuZvQU</a>\n</p><p><i>~Education, the Study of Everything</i>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by OmegaLearn\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/M4Ffhp9NLKY?t=923\">https://youtu.be/M4Ffhp9NLKY?t=923</a>\n</p><p>~ pi_is_3.14\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Punxsutawney_Phil\">Video Solution by Punxsutawney Phil</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Punxsutawney Phil\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtube.com/watch?v=vCEJzhDRUoU\">https://youtube.com/watch?v=vCEJzhDRUoU</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn_.28Vieta.27s_Formula.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn_(Vieta's_Formula)\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn (Vieta's Formula)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by OmegaLearn (Vieta&#39;s Formula)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/afrGHNo_JcY\">https://youtu.be/afrGHNo_JcY</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Hawk_Math\">Video Solution by Hawk Math</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Hawk Math\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=p4iCAZRUESs\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=p4iCAZRUESs</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B\" title=\"2021 AMC 12B\">2021 AMC 12B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2021 AMC 12B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2021 AMC 12B Answer Key\